systemMargins:systemDistance:topSystemDistance:systemDividers:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTenths":{"title":"MXLTenths","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltenths","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tenths type is a number representing tenths of interline staff space (positive or negative). Both integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decimal values are allowed, such as 5 for a half space and 2.5 for a quarter space. Interline space is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the middle of a staff line."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemMargins":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemmargins","title":"MXLSystemMargins","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemMargins","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSystemMargins","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"System margins are relative to the page margins. Positive values indent and negative values reduce the margin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemMargins"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemLayout":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system is a group of staves that are read and played simultaneously. System layout includes left and right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"margins and the vertical distance from the previous system. The system distance is measured from the bottom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line of the previous system to the top line of the current system. It is ignored for the first system on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"page. The top system distance is measured from the page’s top margin to the top line of the first system. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is ignored for all but the first system on a page."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLSystemLayout","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemDividers":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The system-dividers element indicates the presence or absence of system dividers (also known as system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"separation marks) between systems displayed on the same page. Dividers on the left and right side of the page"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are controlled by the left-divider and right-divider elements respectively. The default vertical position is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"half the system-distance value from the top of the system that is below the divider. The default horizontal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position is the left and right system margin, respectively."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemDividers","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLSystemDividers","navigat